{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7pAhAVnrLj9NPkf92S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KVeKwsW6XgMgqnX6nCYetb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184315__x1295cd/work/KarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-184315 && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='data/about.json'; a=json.load(open(p))\na['sourceInformation']['online']='AI Hub shared-world session, Kachinuki, 2-4 players (host runs the bouts; the hub harness passes 4 configurations); local versus 1-2 players on one keyboard; local Kachinuki 3-4 seats with CPU rivals beyond the keyboard player'\na['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless Node suites (59 checks: data, technique, bout, AI, bonus, flow, modes, story playthrough of all 17 nodes, dev), browser screenshots, the AI Hub harness (4 configurations)'\na['testingFeedback'][0]=\"About 12 issues were caught by the early tests, screenshots and playthrough runs. Most were logic and wiring faults (a missing alias that broke boot, a dev scene field overwritten, a drill that matched the wrong technique, a fighter with no personality).\"\na['testingFeedback'].append(\"Later, the hub harness and the modes suite caught a parser error on my side (wrong field names) and a title/attract loop assumption; both fixed.\")\na['engineFeedback'][1]=\"Stuck or guessed wrong: game.go is a fade, so a state read right after it is one second early; the store returns false with no storage, so I added a memory fallback.\"\njson.dump(a,open(p,'w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs | tail -1 && node -e \"const j=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8'));console.log(Object.keys(j), j.testingFeedback.length, j.engineFeedback.length, j.promptFeedback.length)\"","description":"Update the About and exit-interview data and rebuild"},"caller":{"type