{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh86kUrHNqkie4s7pCqN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't meet the goal's last condition from this environment. The one open item is testing the gamepad path and the four-human local setup on real controllers, and I have no hardware here. Everything else in TASK.md is implemented and covered by checks, so the remaining gap is verification on hardware, not missing features.\n\n**Files**\n- Bundle: `KarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-184315.html` in the work folder. It is one file with no external requests.\n- `exit-interview.json` in the same folder. It parses and has all five sections.\n- Dev folder: `KarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-184315/`.\n\n**Checks**\n- `node tests/run.mjs`: 78 passed, 0 failed. Suites: data, input, technique, bout, AI, bonus, flow, modes, pads, audio, UI, story playthrough, dev.\n- The input and UI suites are now written. The earlier pause-menu check always passed, so I removed it.\n- AI Hub harness, final build: all four configurations pass (2 players, 4 players with latency/loss, host-leave, server role). The game draws its own online card, and the Enter-answers-Ready check passes.\n- No TODO, FIXME, or placeholder text in `src/`.\n\n**Still open**\n- Real-controller testing of the pad path and four-human local play (keyboard, keyboard, two pads). The pad input is tested with a stubbed gamepad only.\n- Joint-based hit boxes. The plan asks for them, but TASK.md doesn't; hits use distance and height rules.\n- The plan's broader test set: there's no separate fake-hub online suite and no filmstrip review.\n- Balance: the level-3 CPU Ebi still beats the level-10 autopilot, so the scripted playthrough uses the P1-invincible dev toggle.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-03 18:43:15\n- Source: Karate Champ (1984 arcade, Data East; Japanese title Karate Do)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and perspective: 1-on-1 point-sparring karate fighting with arcade bonus stages; 2D side view, with an optional 2.5D tatami view\n- Tech: my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (handoff package, unmodified), AI Hub client 1.4.0 (unmodified), Web Audio; Node 24 and Python Playwright for tests\n- Art direction: engine Humanoid rigs as PS1-style pixel art at 320×240, with custom stage backdrops\n- Animation: engine rig driven from the fight state, with E.MOVES adapted for the karate techniques\n- Audio: code-generated sequencer music and sound effects; gibberish formant voices in Web Audio\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world session, Kachinuki, 2–4 players; the game draws its own card; local versus 1–2 players; local Kachinuki with up to 4 humans\n- Testing: 78 headless checks, a scripted playthrough of all 17 ladder nodes, browser screenshots, and the AI Hub harness (4 configurations)\n- Research: the summary in PLAN.md §1.1 only\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- About 12 issues were caught early, four of them breaking: a boot failure, a practice-scene crash, a Dev-mode crash, and a headless save that kept nothing. All four are fixed.\n- Later, the hub harness and the modes suite caught my own parser error and an attract-loop assumption. I also caught a wrong count in my own input check and a placeholder check that always passed. All are fixed.\n- Most helpful: the scripted whole-ladder playthrough, which crossed every scene transition at once.\n- Least helpful: the 20-seed balance probe, which mostly showed the random stream dominating results.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked: the Humanoid rig, the Backdrop and Dialog helpers, and `game.advance` with `draw`, which made scene checks possible.\n- Stuck: `game.go` fades, so state read right after it is a second early. The store returns false with no storage, so I added a memory fallback in the game.\n- Built myself: the fight simulation, the CPU, the bonus rules, the drills, the online Kachinuki, the Technique Lab, the pad input, and the voice synth.\n- Hardest: pushing the fight state into the rig each step without drawing on every frame, while keeping that state serializable for online guests.\n- Engine changes: none.\n- One change I'd want: an in-memory store fallback so headless tests can use the same save path.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked: the staged structure (read STAGE.md, with TASK.md winning over PLAN.md) and the explicit done-when list.\n- Confusing: the plan's opus-max file names against TASK.md's haiku-medium names, and a plan scope that one session can't finish.\n- Hardest: the online netcode and the harness wiring, which both need exact protocol detail.\n- Change: name the must-have features for a first build, and the expected test counts. Also say whether real-controller testing is expected when no hardware is available."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":757,"cache_read_input_tokens":484515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":757},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14f34045-19a9-4c91-b4b0-8ef52e3ad772","uuid":"cb305454-7520-4faf-a6a4-45036795ff3a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:46:50.830Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh86kDUUSMyFhryrUXge"}
